# Paired runner: intend.ncl
# Verb:          intend
#
# Semantics: North-star contractile. Declares BOTH concrete committed
#            next-actions AND horizon aspirations the project wishes to
#            become. Two sections share one file because they answer
#            the same question at different ranges:
#              [[intents]] — "we WILL do this; track progress"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → done |
#                                    deferred | retired
#              [[wishes]]  — "we WISH this were true; revisit later"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → achieved |
#                                    abandoned
#                            grouped by horizon: near / mid / far.
#            Non-gating — this is a report, not a gate. See the `must`
#            contractile for hard gates.

@abstract:
North-star contractile for Skein.jl: a standalone knot-database library
for Julia (scope per docs/decisions/ADR-0001 — one master, general Julia
users; QuandleDB/KRL/Tangle are consumers).
@end

## Purpose

Skein.jl makes knot persistence a solved problem for Julia: store knots as
Gauss codes (or canonical planar diagrams via the optional KnotTheory.jl
extension), get invariants computed and indexed automatically on insert, and
query, compare, import and export them through a small composable API.

## Anti-Purpose

This repository is NOT:
- The engine/substrate of the KRL stack (withdrawn — ADR-0001); QuandleDB/KRL
  are consumers, and consumption defines neither purpose nor architecture
- An ABI/FFI showcase or a coprocessor/accelerator demo (both removed as
  vestigial; see .machine_readable/rsr-profile.a2ml)
- A replacement for KnotTheory.jl (it persists and caches what KnotTheory computes)
- A general-purpose database engine (the schema is knot-shaped by design)

## If In Doubt

If you are unsure whether a change is in scope, ask. Sensitive areas:
- src/storage.jl schema and migrations
- Project.toml dependency additions (estate packages need an ADR)
- .machine_readable/ estate manifests (6a2/, contractiles/)

## Committed Next-Actions

### standalone-install
- description: Pkg.add(url=...) works with no sibling checkouts; tests green on the CI matrix
- probe: .github/workflows/ci.yml has no AcceleratorGate step and Matrix is 1.10/1.11
- status: done
- notes: 0.4.0 — KnotTheory restored to weakdep-only; Manifest uncommitted

### vestigial-jettison
- description: ABI/FFI seam and accelerator extensions removed; profile recorded
- probe: test -f .machine_readable/rsr-profile.a2ml && ! test -d src/abi
- status: done
- notes: ADR-0001; DUST entries in contractiles/dust/Dustfile.a2ml

### general-registry
- description: Register in the Julia General registry (install by name)
- probe: Pkg.add("Skein") resolves without url=
- status: declared
- notes: requires KnotTheory.jl registration path decided first (it is the weakdep)

### query-contract-hardening
- description: property tests cover every column in the INTEGRATION.adoc query contract
- probe: test/property_test.jl names each guaranteed column
- status: in_progress

